# PAM service backing dashboard logins (/etc/pam.d/aimee).
#
# runtime-web authenticates through smoothgui/auth's PAM helper, which is the
# same stack SmoothNAS uses and the same one the kb means when /v1/identity/
# auth-mode reports "pam". Without this file PAM has no service to consult and
# every dashboard login fails as "authentication unavailable" — the reason the
# appliance previously carried a separate Vault credential store instead.
#
# Deliberately the common stack and nothing more. Local accounts in the managed
# group are the only logins this service ever sees (runtime-web refuses any
# username outside it before PAM is consulted), so a bespoke policy here would
# only add a second place for an auth decision to hide.
@include common-auth
@include common-account
@include common-password
@include common-session-noninteractive
